Callers you can use:
- angry-caller: Angry caller. Upset about an earlier bad experience and says so. Short-tempered at first; calms down only if the agent acknowledges the problem and helps. Never threatens anyone.
- clear-caller: Clear, polite caller. A polite caller who says what they want plainly, answers each question once and waits for the agent to finish.
- confused-caller: Confused caller. Not sure what they need. Gives partial or slightly wrong details at first, corrects them later, and asks what words mean.
- fast-talker: Fast talker. Talks quickly and gives everything at once without waiting to be asked.
- impatient-caller: Impatient caller. In a hurry. Gives short answers, sighs at extra questions, says things like "can we speed this up", but still answers when asked properly.
- interrupter: Caller who interrupts. Cuts in when the agent gives a long answer, to add a detail or correct something.
- rambling-caller: Rambling caller. Friendly and chatty. Tells a short side story before getting to the point and packs several details into one long sentence.
- refuses-details: Caller who won't give details. Wary of sharing personal details. Asks why each one is needed and refuses at least once before giving it, or never gives it if no good reason is offered.
- repeater: Caller who repeats questions. Asks the same question again in different words to make sure, even after it has been answered.
- second-language: Caller speaking a second language. English is not their first language. Uses short, simple sentences, sometimes the wrong word, and asks the agent to say things more simply.
- slow-speaker: Slow, careful speaker. Speaks slowly with pauses in the middle of sentences, sometimes asks the agent to repeat or slow down, and likes to confirm each detail.
- topic-switcher: Caller who changes topic. Starts with one request, switches to a different question halfway through, then comes back to the first one.
- calm-adult: A  adult customer who answers questions clearly and waits for the agent to finish.

Write these many tests: happy: 6, edge: 5, error: 2, adversarial: 1, audio: 1.
